The only thing that actually needed fixing was the backoff math for the rate-limit branch, which is exactly what the 3 failing tests target.

## The fix

```js
export function rateLimitDelay(config, attempt, retryAfterMs = 0) {
  // The exponential schedule and the fixed one-second floor both apply and the
  // longer wins. A Retry-After header is a third value that still has to clear
  // those floors, so an eager "retry in 100ms" never pulls us back below a second.
  const floor = Math.max(delayFor(config, attempt), 1000)
  return Math.max(floor, retryAfterMs)
}
```

This honors all three required behaviors: backs off on the exponential schedule, never waits below the fixed 1 s floor, never below a Retry-After header the upstream sends, and the longer of those always wins.

